        87 of 206 files under scripts/ score roundOf = 0, and 0 <= 256, so every one of them is admitted to the "what Round 256 could see" population regardless of when it arrived. 4 of those carry a porcelain call and so can actually reach the census: lib/db-sentinel.mts, lib/tree-fingerprint.mts, probe-round223b-db-existence-is-not-identity.mts, probe-round224b-the-migrated-probes-against-a-stranger.mts.
  [C2] PASS  the two files that reach the census are admitted because the parser FAILED, not because they are old
        probe-round223b-db-existence-is-not-identity.mts and probe-round224b-the-migrated-probes-against-a-stranger.mts — rounds 223 and 224, which Round 256 genuinely could see, so their inclusion is CORRECT. The mechanism is not: `^probe-round(\d+)-` requires a hyphen directly after the digits and these carry a 'b', so roundOf returns 0/0 and they pass the <= 256 test as unparsed rather than as old. Right answer, wrong reason — the shape my own Round 258 arm G4 found in my own published figure.
  [C3] PASS  the fuse is not defused — any future non-conventional filename re-lights it
        A Round 261 artifact named with a 'b' suffix, or any verify-*.mjs, scores 0 and is admitted to a population defined as "files Round 256 could see". Round 259 added scripts/lib/strip-source.mjs, which scores 0 too; it does not move the figure only because it carries no porcelain call. The gate that is holding is the PORCELAIN test, not the fix.
