        Population = git ls-tree at 6465346a (the commit that ADDED probe-round256), minus that probe itself — 137 files, 137 still present today. Reading today's bytes: tree pin 13 comparing / 10 asserting, heuristic 13 / 10. The two instruments agree, which is the argument; the figure itself is today's and is NOT pinned — C5 says why, and C6 holds the literal over the population where a literal survives. This arm read "13 / 10" until 2026-09-24, when the fleet moved underneath it exactly as C5 predicted.
  [C5] MEAS  the second axis is live and unpinned
